KW  - Nannochloropsis oceanica
KW  - Dual-ligand metal-MOF
KW  - METAL-ORGANIC FRAMEWORK
KW  - POLAR GROUPS
AB  - To overcome the limited CO2 bioavailability and low fixation efficiency in microalgal systems, a dual-ligand MOF, NH2-MIL-125/Zn, was constructed and integrated with Nannochloropsis oceanica to form a bio-hybrid platform. The material exhibited enhanced surface area, CO2 adsorption capacity, and favorable interfacial properties for microalgal attachment. Under 10% CO2, the optimal 8 mg/L treatment increased biomass (24.85%), lipid content (76.8%), and lipid productivity (137%) compared to the control. Carbon fixation performance was also significantly improved. Mechanistic analysis revealed that NH2-MIL-125/Zn enhanced CO2 enrichment and activated carbon metabolism by increasing Rubisco and ACCase activities and upregulating rbcL, psbA, and LACS expression, thereby redirecting carbon flux toward lipid biosynthesis. This study provides a synergistic strategy for improving CO2 utilization and biofuel production via MOF-microalgae hybrid systems.
